    "interpretation": [
      "Mean step wall time exceeds the 10 ms budget. The timer is not the only source of the observed slowdown.",
      "The camera-off control reached approximately 1.0 RTF while the comparable baseline with cameras was approximately 0.63. Rendering and visual-state activity share resources with main control/physics.",
      "Command/physics section timers include waits for GPU work; they do not isolate arm arithmetic or pure Genesis kernel execution.",
      "Same-host Sim-to-Pilot DDS message age was approximately 2 ms median. WAN/UI end-to-end latency was not measured.",
      "Telemetry follows simulation-time cadence: at about 0.64 RTF, its measured median interval was about 76 ms.",
      "Fixed-clock cadence regression emits 250 frames over 10 wall seconds at 100 steps/s and 180 at 60 steps/s after the deadline fix. These are scheduling tests, not measured media receive FPS.",
      "The isolated GPU visual-worker trial improved one sequential full-runtime comparison modestly, while CPU pose with GPU GL rendering did not produce a meaningful gain and was rejected.",
      "No paired trial combined all accepted patches. Full-runtime comparisons were candidate then reference, not randomized; host load and startup transients limit causal effect-size claims."
    ]
  },
  "accepted_changes": [
    "Authoritative arm/claw velocity reset uses skip_forward and the following position write performs one coherent FK; base/leg velocities preserved.",
    "Visual-only camera replicas defer root changes to the joint FK and cache exact unchanged snapshot values per epoch.",
    "Camera deadline always advances beyond a due slot even under floating-point rounding; no accumulating backlog.",
    "Map go2_pympc_solve timing events to the existing canonical go2_mpc_solve fields with per-event averaging."
  ],
  "rejected_experiments": [
    "CPU pose backend plus one Torch CPU thread in camera replicas, while keeping NVIDIA GL/NVENC and 1280x720; no meaningful full-runtime gain, not included in source.",
    "Static Genesis performance mode was measured separately but left at the existing false default; not part of the patch."
  ],
